# NON-EXECUTABLE ANNOTATED MALBOLGE MODULE SCAFFOLD.
#
# Module: doom.host.v1.windows
# Generated-from: cli/adapters/doom/windows.c
# Intended artifact: cli/adapters/doom/windows.malbolge
#
# This file intentionally contains no canonical Malbolge bytes yet. It reserves
# the Windows runner module identity while preserving the architecture boundary:
# Win32 system calls remain host-runner capabilities and are never encoded as
# guest pointers, host ABIs, or hidden native callbacks inside doom.malbolge.
#
# Runtime rule: on supported Windows hosts, a .malbolge capsule declaring
# doom.host.v1 must resolve this adapter automatically after loading
# doom.host.v1.abi. The same doom.malbolge payload must select Linux/macOS host
# adapters without changing guest bytes.
#
# Mouse capture is guest-directed: gameplay requests centered relative capture;
# pause, menus, automap, demos, and focus loss release it. Execution telemetry is
# language-neutral, so the title may show either C source lines during native
# debugging or Malbolge cell/address plus active graphical instruction.
#
# Blocked by: versioned-host-capability-call-abi, state-aware-malbolge-linker,
# cross-platform-native-capability-runners, and C-to-Malbolge code generation.
